course: dictionary
lesson: 9024
title: Skylight: a window in the roof
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A skylight is a window set in a roof or ceiling, so daylight comes in from above. The word has two clues: sky, which is above you, and light, which is what comes through.
explain: «When big hailstones fall, go indoors and stay away from windows and skylights, because hail can hurt people and break glass.» Skylights sit next to windows in this sentence, and the glass is what can break, so a skylight must be a window too, one that is up in the roof.
explain: «Old roofs often have skylights and thin panels that break when stepped on.» This tells you not to walk on one. A window is not a floor. To check your meaning, swap it in: a window in the roof that lets daylight in makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A skylight is a window in a roof or ceiling.
fact: Skylights let daylight in from above.
fact: Skylights can break if someone steps on them, so never walk on one.
fact: Hail can break glass, so in a hailstorm go indoors and stay away from skylights.
fact: Old skylights can look solid when they are not.
exercise: What is a skylight? | A thin metal ladder | A kind of lamp that runs on electricity | A floor you can walk on | *A window in a roof or ceiling that lets daylight in
exercise: «When big hailstones fall, go indoors and stay away from windows and skylights.» Why? | Skylights are warm and cosy | *Hail can hurt people and break glass | Skylights make the room too hot | Hail makes the sky light up
exercise: «Old roofs often have skylights and thin panels that break when stepped on.» Find and copy the word that tells you what breaks when stepped on. | old | *panels | roofs | often
test: «The skylight let bright sunshine into the attic.» What does skylight mean? | *A window in the roof | A door in the floor | A kind of cloud | A dark cupboard
test: Why should you never walk on an old skylight? | It may be the way to the attic | *Its thin panels can break, and you could fall | It is too shiny | It makes your shoes wet
exam: Which is the best way to check the meaning of a new word? | Guess the first meaning you think of | Skip every hard word and never come back to it | Ask someone to say it loudly | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
